From cf9d2f18d3342d99e69fe570295f9c0febe2ebad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mahran Rezk <mahranrezk10@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 22:56:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add passive input availability monitor (no output change)

First step towards #4 (degraded-mode fallback). This commit only observes;
synchronization, fusion and publishing are unchanged.

- InputAvailabilityMonitor: per-input UNKNOWN/HEALTHY/STALE/RECOVERING and
  aggregate NOMINAL/DEGRADED/INSUFFICIENT state derived from arrival times,
  plus timing statistics (inter-arrival gaps, silences, detection latency,
  recovery time, header stamp anomalies). Plain C++ without ROS types,
  unit-tested with fake time.
- One const arrival observer per input, registered before the synchronizer,
  and a 10 ms evaluator timer on the node clock, created last in setup().
- New read-only parameter degraded_mode.input_timeout (default 0.3 s,
  provisional). Transitions and a periodic summary are logged at DEBUG
  level only.
- Declare message_filters as a dependency: the node header already includes
  it directly, and the new test uses it.

Tests: state machine unit tests, including a scripted trace checked against
the reference model; message_filters tests showing that a const observer
receives the published object itself (no copy) and does not change the
ApproximateTime output.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
